; Many asks to one structure (D183). Each ask forks a box that monitors
; the structure, and ends once it has the answer, and its monitor goes
; with it. Before, every box's monitor stayed on the structure, and each
; new one walked them all to get to the end, so these 100,000 asks took
; minutes; now they take as long as the asks. A counter in a cell, read
; and set 100,000 times. (Under SLIGHT_GC_STRESS, which collects at every
; recv, it needs n of about 1,000 to finish in time.)

(@include :ds)

(defun count-up (c n)
    (cond
        ((== n 0) (cell/get c))
        (#true    (cell/set c (+ (cell/get c) 1)) (count-up c (- n 1)))))

(count-up (cell/new 0) 100000)
